    family-names: "Hendrick"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    website: "https://github.com/ChaseHendrick"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9754-6087"
# GENChase itself is not deposited on Zenodo and has no software DOI.
# Paper preprint DOIs belong in the references below.
version: "0.7.1"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChaseHendrick/GENChase"
url: "https://github.com/ChaseHendrick/GENChase"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/ChaseHendrick/GENChase/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  GENChase is a development and research working environment. Its art and print
  studio is a folder-based browser studio with one shared engine and
  135 pattern-forming systems from physics, chemistry, biology and mathematics,
  each implemented as a real simulation rather than as a style applied to
  noise. A portable single-file HTML build is also included. Every plate is
  deterministic from a seed, reconstructible from a URL hash, and exportable at
  print resolution in inches, as vectors where the picture is discrete marks.
  Most techniques measure a quantity that theory predicts, from the field
  currently on screen, and print it alongside the value theory gives. The
  formulas behind the tabs three-vortex-bound, parallelogram-lock,
  quincunx-lock and double-triangle-bound are proved in the paper "Minimal
  Winding in the Self-Similar Collapse of Point Vortices", with zero confirmed
  novel findings (identities/NOVELTY-AUDIT.md). The first specializes
  Gröbli’s 1877 spiral coefficient and is the ratio of the rates Kimura gives
  in J. Phys. Soc. Jpn. 56 (1987), Eq. (4.4).
keywords:
  - generative art
  - scientific visualization
  - simulation
  - reaction-diffusion
  - pattern formation
  - WebGL
  - partial differential equations
  - random matrix theory
  - hyperbolic geometry
  - landscape evolution
  - active matter
  - Bose-Einstein condensate
  - cellular Potts model
  - KPZ universality
  - neural field theory
  - print
  - point vortex collapse
